  "closed_events": 47,
  "method": "Decode the F4 and F5 displays before and after one completed Queue Desk task. Compare the count and visible digest on each view. Use the serial output and exit note to reconstruct the three task records. The two subsequent system-state records link the last full F4 head to the final digest printed during shutdown. Times and the spent-period field were reconstructed where no screen displayed them. Hash links are over sorted compact JSON without a trailing newline.",
  "coverage": "At 320x200, 640x480, 1280x720, 1920x1080 and 2560x1440 all 64 digits were displayed and all five hash links reproduced. At 800x600 and 1024x768 only the marked 21- and 43-digit prefixes, the common F5 digits and the event counts were tested.",
  "controls": "A pre-launch register paired with a post-launch verification, and the reverse, were rejected in all seven guests. At the five full-head sizes the replay changes the last hex digit of the last F4 head using a valid glyph. The visible F5 prefix stays the same but the recalculated shutdown digest disagrees.",
  "replay_note": "The first offline last-digit control assumed the final 12 digits fit on one row. It stopped at 640x480. The corrected replay tracks the end of the wrapped field; original guest captures were preserved.",
